  "partition_distance_note": "d_P is the partition distance of src/qec_transversal/faulttolerance.py: the minimum, over logical operators, of the number of cells their support meets. One unflagged faulty gate is correctable exactly when d_P >= 3. It is decided here by the exhaustive two-cell search, so every verdict is certified. Cell width alone settles nothing: d_P >= ceil(d / width) is the only general relation."
